Z||000007||MsBeth||09-19-2001||01:01 AM||||I was watching ... for a guy who has made me laugh for 20 years .... he brought me to tears with his pain and confusion.<P>Dave was amazing tonight too... Dennis Leary was on - he has a "fund" started because of his cousin (a firefighter) who died in the big fire in 99 in Wocester MA.  The "fund" has been expanded to include the families of the firefighters who lost their lives because of what happened 9/11/01.  <P><BR>MsBeth<P>Side Note :<BR>There are fire stations that have no equiptment...NONE - how can they do their jobs without the tools they need ???  They can't.  All the equiptment was lost when the towers came down.<P>||||reg||1
Z||000008||firstfiero||09-19-2001||10:37 AM||||    I must agree. I've have been watching dave for years. I must say that was probobly the most moving speech on the current situation I have seen. You could really tell how much he loves the city. He was choking back tears more the once during his monologue.<P>------------------<BR><BR>   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/firstfiero.gif"> ||||reg||1
